curfew-sidebar: que's sidebar for the herdr app.

workspace.mjs ports parts of que (https://github.com/queapp-org/que), by the same
author, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
(https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0): the workspace name word lists and
their drawing (src/shared/names.ts); the new-workspace steps of
src/daemon/workspaces.ts (the name clash check, fetchOrigin, detectDefaultBranch,
addWorktree and copyIncludes); and the que.toml and .worktreeinclude rules of
src/shared/config.ts, read by a small reader of its own for setup, default_branch
and worktree_include. main.js draws que's sidebar (src/renderer/src/components/
Sidebar.tsx and WorkingMark.tsx, docs/design.md), the preparing row included.
titles.mjs ports que's session names: the label a Claude Code session writes to its
terminal title (src/shared/session-label.ts, capTitle of src/shared/brief.ts) and
the rule that it names its workspace (src/daemon/workspaces.ts, labelFromSession).
remove.mjs and main.js remove a project que's way: the dialog's words
(RemoveProjectDialog in src/renderer/src/components/dialogs.tsx, drawn by
mods/curfew-project) and the removal order of WorkspaceManager.removeProject and its
removal steps (src/daemon/workspaces.ts): the terminals first, then each worktree
removed by force and pruned, the branches kept. Here deleting the worktrees is
opt-in, only those under ~/.herdr/worktrees go, and each is checked against git's
list again right before.

The helpers that find where a space is now (base, place, where) are adapted from
the Herdr app's shipped spaces mod (Apache-2.0). remove.mjs reads `git worktree list
--porcelain` and checks for uncommitted changes (git status without optional locks
or fsmonitor) as the Herdr app's shipped worktree mod does (Apache-2.0).
